```

## Example Session Summary

```markdown
# Session 2 Summary: Phase 1 (POST /posts)

## Overview
Implemented blog post creation endpoint with full Prisma database integration, authentication, and E2E testing.

## Implementation Details

### Database Changes
- Added Post model to prisma/schema.prisma
- Migration applied: 20240101000000_create_posts_table
- Added index on authorId and createdAt

### Schemas Created
- PostBaseSchema (src/schemas/post.schema.ts): Business fields only
- PostSchema (src/schemas/post.schema.ts): Full schema with id + timestamps
- PostCreateSchema (src/schemas/post.schema.ts): Creation schema
- PostUpdateSchema (src/schemas/post.schema.ts): Update schema (all fields optional)
- CreatePostRequestSchema (src/schemas/post.schema.ts): API request schema
- PostResponseSchema (src/schemas/post.schema.ts): API response schema

### Repository Methods
- PostRepository.create() - Create new post
- PostRepository.toModel() - Typed mapper from Prisma row to domain model
- File: src/repositories/post.repository.ts

### Service Layer
- PostService.createPost() - Business logic for post creation
- Includes error handling and logging
- File: src/services/post.service.ts

### API Endpoint
- POST /api/posts
- Request: CreatePostRequestSchema (title, content)
- Response: PostResponseSchema (postId, title, content, authorId, createdAt)
- Authentication: Required (JWT Bearer token)
- File: src/routes/posts.ts, src/controllers/posts.controller.ts

## Tests

### E2E Tests
- tests/routes/posts.test.ts::creates a post - Success case
- tests/routes/posts.test.ts::rejects invalid input - Validation errors
- tests/routes/posts.test.ts::requires authentication - Auth requirement
- All tests passing: YES

### Unit Tests
- tests/services/post.service.test.ts - Service layer with mocked repository
- Coverage: 95% of service methods

## Shared Libraries

### Available for Next Sessions
- PostRepository - Can be used for GET /posts/{id} in Session 3
- PostService - Can be extended with getById() method
- Post schema - Represents core post entity

### Dependencies
- No new packages added
- No new environment variables needed

## Known Limitations

### Current Implementation
- Only creation implemented, no read/update/delete yet
- No support for tags or categories
- No content length validation beyond Zod
- No duplicate post prevention

### Technical Debt
- Consider adding content sanitization
- May need to add a post status field (draft/published)
- Service layer could accept an injected PrismaClient for easier testing

## Next Phase Recommendations

### Suggested Next Session
Session 3: Phase 2 (GET /posts/{id})
- Depends on Session 2 (need posts to read)
- Simple implementation (reuse PostRepository)
- High user value (view created posts)
- Session plan: plan/sessions/session-3-phase-2.md

### Prerequisite Work
- Add PostRepository.getById() method
- Add PostService.getPostById() method
- Add GET route to src/routes/posts.ts
- Write E2E test for retrieval

## Learnings and Gotchas

### What Worked Well
- Layered Zod schema architecture prevented confusion
- Typed repository mappers caught field name mismatches early
- TDD approach caught an authentication middleware bug early
- Service layer made unit testing straightforward

### Challenges Encountered
- Initial confusion about which layer owns Zod parsing (controller, not service)
- Needed to ensure Prisma's `Date` fields were serialized to ISO strings
- Test fixtures required unique emails per test run

### Time Estimates
- Estimated time: 25 minutes
- Actual time: 30 minutes
- Variance: +5 minutes for debugging date serialization

## Code Quality Metrics

### Formatting
- Prettier applied: YES
- Explicit return type coverage: 100%
- TSDoc comments added: YES

### Testing
- E2E test coverage: 3 scenarios
- Unit test coverage: 95%
- All tests passing: YES

## Files Changed

### Created
- src/schemas/post.schema.ts
- src/repositories/post.repository.ts
- src/services/post.service.ts
- src/controllers/posts.controller.ts
- src/routes/posts.ts
- tests/routes/posts.test.ts
- tests/services/post.service.test.ts
- prisma/migrations/20240101000000_create_posts_table/migration.sql

### Modified
- src/app.ts (registered posts router)
- prisma/schema.prisma (added Post model)
- package.json (no changes)
- .env.example (no changes)

### Deleted
- None
```

## Session Transition Checklist

Before generating summary and moving to next session:

### Code Quality
- [ ] All E2E tests passing
- [ ] All unit tests passing
- [ ] Code formatted with Prettier
- [ ] Explicit return types on all exported functions
- [ ] TSDoc comments on all public APIs
- [ ] No linting errors (eslint)
- [ ] No type checking errors (tsc --noEmit)

### Documentation
- [ ] Code comments for complex logic
- [ ] README updated if needed
- [ ] API documentation (openapi.yaml) updated
- [ ] Migration files documented

### Testing
- [ ] E2E test for success case
- [ ] E2E test for error cases
- [ ] E2E test for authentication
- [ ] Unit tests for complex business logic
- [ ] Test coverage adequate

### Implementation
- [ ] Feature complete per session requirements
- [ ] Error handling implemented
- [ ] Logging added
- [ ] No hardcoded values
- [ ] Secrets properly managed

### Knowledge Transfer
- [ ] Shared libraries documented
- [ ] Dependencies documented
- [ ] Known limitations listed
- [ ] Next session recommendations provided
- [ ] Session plan objectives met

## Generating the Session Summary

When user says "Session N complete" or "Transition to next session":

1. Read current session implementation
2. Analyze all changes made
3. Generate comprehensive summary
4. Save to plan/sessions/session-N-summary.md
5. Provide brief verbal summary to user
6. Ask for confirmation before proceeding

## Session Kickoff

When starting a new session:

1. Read previous session summaries
2. Review next session plan (plan/sessions/session-N-phase-M.md)
3. Identify available shared libraries
4. Check dependencies
5. Confirm session requirements with user
6. Begin with E2E test writing

## Research Export

When encountering issues requiring external research:

Generate research-export.md using templates/research-export.md:
- Document the problem clearly
- List all attempted solutions
- Include relevant code snippets
- Formulate specific questions
- Provide context from phase summaries

## Continuous Improvement

After each session:
- Update time estimates based on actual time
- Note patterns that worked well
- Document challenges for future reference
- Suggest process improvements
- Update session plans for future projects

## Session Transition Anti-Patterns

Do NOT:
- Move to next session with failing tests
- Skip session summary generation
- Document only what was built (also document why)
- Forget to note known limitations
- Skip recommendations for next session
- Generate summary without reading code
- Use generic summaries (be specific)
- Forget to document shared libraries
- Skip session plan review
- Automatically start next session
- Combine multiple sessions into one
